FIX Collection autoplay sub-pixel accumulation bug. In /app/frontend/src/components/sections/Collection.jsx replace `el.scrollLeft += SPEED` with a virtual position accumulator. Suggested fix:
  let pos = 0;
  const tick = () => {
    if (el.scrollWidth > el.clientWidth) {
      pos += SPEED;
      const half = el.scrollWidth / 2;
      if (pos >= half) pos -= half;
      el.scrollLeft = pos;  // browsers floor on read but a fresh write each frame is fine when the source value is monotonic
    }
    rafRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  };
Alternatively bump SPEED to >=1 (e.g. SPEED=1, 60px/sec) — but the accumulator approach is more robust and lets you keep slow drift. Verify by running `scrollLeft` poll in DevTools — should advance ~27px/sec.
